# generated build artifacts
# NOTE: version.cst is deliberately NOT here. It is what `caustic-mk --version`
# reports and what `version_file` keeps in sync, so a clean clone has to carry
# it — exactly like the parent repo's src/version.cst. It used to be ignored
# because an older build step generated it into the source tree unasked.
*.cst.s
*.cst.s.o
.caustic/

# build outputs (out_dir, and the per-triple directories under it)
build/

# the maker builds itself here
/caustic-mk
/caustic-mk.exe
# CodeView debug data, written beside a windows-x86_64 build
*.pdb

# test scratch. integration.sh works on copies in $TMPDIR, so a clean checkout
# never grows these — they only appear when a fixture is run in place by hand.
tests/tmp/
tests/fixtures/*/build/
tests/fixtures/*/dist/
